","[#083eb]_#_[#045b8]","[#083eb]_#_[#b81d3]"],"description":"Whenever SpikerBot sees the color red, an inhibitory signal will stop all of SpikerBot\u2019s actions, and prevent them from starting, until red is removed from Spikerbot\u2019s vision.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775500431578","neuronKeys":["[#3b386]","[#b81d3]","[#045b8]","[#083eb]"],"edgeStrings":["[#3b386]_#_[#b81d3]","[#3b386]_#_[#06f17]","[#3b386]_#_[#16759]","[#b81d3]_#_[#3b386]","[#782a6]_#_[#083eb]","[#782a6]_#_[#045b8]","[#083eb]_#_[#3b386]","[#083eb]_#_[#045b8]","[#083eb]_#_[#b81d3]","[#045b8]_#_[#b81d3]","[#b81d3]_#_[#9e98c]","[#b81d3]_#_[#eac80]"],"description":"What can you add, remove, or modify to make yourSpikerBot win in a game of \u201cred light, green light\u201d?","thumbnail":""}],"info":{"title":"Red Light Green Light","description":"SpikerBot rushes forward when it sees green, and stops when it sees red. Try racing multiple SpikerBots!","author":"User","version":"1.0.1","timestamp":"2026-04-08T15:36:01.141205"}}